Minimal portability patches to build the vendored 2026-TR AnyPIA source with
modern clang/libc++. Applied by oracle/build/Makefile to the work tree after
CRLF->LF normalization; oracle/vendor/ is never modified.

1. linux/BitAnnual{.cpp,Inlines.h}: the class member is `theData` (BitAnnual.h)
   but the published linux files still reference `data`; also add the copy
   constructor that only the Windows build provided.
2. include/WorkerDataGeneral.h: libc++ bitset::operator[] const returns a
   proxy; use .test() so the static_cast to the Sex enum is legal.
3. linux/CommaBase.h: qualify std::ends.
4. source32/anypiab/{anypiabdoc.h,anypiab.cpp}: include piaout and declare
   TaxData/PiaOut members only under DETAILS (piaout is not vendored), and
   include only the driver header selected by ANYPIAB.

